A project I administer has 2 old DEC 2100's.  They interface via the two
tty ports with a custom piece of equipment.  One is running Ultrix 4.1,
the other Ultrix 4.5.

/dev/tty00 and /dev/tty01 are the devices for the physical tty ports in
back.

To test the ports to ensure that data is being transferred properly to
the custom piece of equipment, a cable is used to connect one tty port
to
the other.  Two xterm's are raised and tipped to the two tty devices,
then
the "~." is typed in the xterm connected to tty01 (does this disconnect
the xterm from the device but leave the tty active?) and an echo command
is redirected to tty01.  The output appears on the other xterm since the
two ports are physically connected in back:

xterm1             xterm2
-----------        -----------
# tip tty00        # tip tty01
connected...       connected...
hello              <return>
     hello         ~.
          hello    [EOT]
                   # echo hello > /dev/tty01
                   # echo hello > /dev/tty01
                   # echo hello > /dev/tty01

This works fine in Ultrix 4.1 but with Ultrix 4.5 the result is like
this:

xterm1             xterm2
-----------        -----------
# tip tty00        # tip tty01
connected...       connected...
ello               <return>
    ello           ~.
        ello       [EOT]
                   # echo hello > /dev/tty01
                   # echo hello > /dev/tty01
                   # echo hello > /dev/tty01

In this case the first letter is dropped.  With other words no letters
are dropped.  With different words certain letters are dropped in one
word but not the other.  It is not always dropping letters in a
particular position.  It is, however, consistent with any particular
word.  I've messed with the tty setting via stty, I've copied the the
/etc/ttys, /etc/termcap and other files from Ultrix 4.1.  Nothing seems
to work.

I have tried not disconnecting (via ~.) in xterm2 and bringing up a
third xterm and doing the "echo hello > /dev/tty01" from there.  All
letters, regarldess of what I echo, are output on xterm1 in this case.

The problem is, because of Y2K issues, both machines must be upgraded to
Ultrix 4.5.  Does anyone have any clue about this?  Please email me at

lpt@msd.ray.com

thanks,
Larry Turowski



