: 
: Jan 31 08:30:37 alpha400 vmunix: tu0: DECchip 21040-AA: Revision: 2.3
: Jan 31 08:30:37 alpha400 vmunix: tu0 at pci0
: Jan 31 08:30:37 alpha400 vmunix: tu0: DEC TULIP Ethernet Interface,
: hardware address: 08-00-2B-E4-0C-A6
: Jan 31 08:30:38 alpha400 vmunix: tu0: selecting 10BaseT port
: 
: I assume I can choose a standard  PCI 10/100Base-T adapter to replace
: the TULIP card.  
: 
: Is there anything in particular one should know about the actual
: replacement procedure?  Is there a makedev or anything weird or
: wonderful to perform?

I'd recommend getting a genuine DE500-BA (a Digital board).  That way, you
know it will work, and won't have to fiddle with it.

As far as getting it to work, since your kernel has support for "tu0", all
you'll need to do is:

        - take out the old card
        - plug the new card in it's place
        - tell the console to configure the card to run at 100Mb:
                >>> set ewa0_mode fast (or FastFD for full duplex)
        - init the console to apply the changes
        - boot the operating system
        
        Stu



