Hi, 

It's been a few months since I did this, but here 
are my notes. 

Assuming: LSM is installed, and kernel rebuilt. Also 
layout on paper the disks pairs to be used if many.

Here are the steps from my notes using two disks as 
an example:

0) using two disks other than the root disk!
1) volinstall
   - sets up the inittab
2) disklabel -rw /dev/rrz1c rz28
   disklabel -rw /dev/rrz2c rz28
3) volsetup
   - creates the LSM structure on the disks
   - enter rz1 and rz2 then return on a blank line
     to continue
4) volassist make volume volume_test 4109967s mirror=yes rz1 rz2
   - replace 4109967s with the 'actual number of sectors's
5) volprint -htA
   - shows the LSM setup
6) newfs /dev/vol/volume_test rz28 
   - create filesytem 
   - I guess you can select UFS or ADVFS here
7) mount the filesystems to a mount point. 
   - add entries to /etc/fstab to mount them on boot

Mike


