I just found out the hard way that the xntpd supplied with DU 4.0D
doesn't seem to bind to any interfaces but the primary - at least as
far as virtual interfaces are concerned.

My goal ws to create three stratum 2 servers for my site, named
ntp-s2-{1,2,3}, each with its own unique IP so it could be moved
transparently. The actual servers are two Solaris 2.6/SPARC and one DU
4.0D (AlphaServer 800) boxes.

On the Suns, there is no problems whatsoever - xntpd happly answers on
_all_ defined physical and virtual interfaces, but on Digital Unix it
only listens on the primary name (the hostname). There is nothing
wrong with the virtual interface either (or IP alias if that is more
correct for Digital Unix) - other network services such as inetd
(telnetd, rlogind, ftpd) or sshd work just fine. I also made sure that
xntpd is started after the alias is created. Netmasks and broadcast
addresses are set to the same values for aliases and physical
interfaces.

Is this a known bug? Any solutions around? I did try to compile a new
distribution, but so far the replacement xntpd just hangs so I have
put that to rest for the moment. For time being I have resorted to
using a CNAME for the DU machine instead.

Thanks,
