|> Re: 126.gcc, you probably need to do "unlimit" if you're in csh or
|> something similar. The defaults do not always allow enough virtual space
|> for the compiler to operate.

Here's some csh stuff I do before running SPEC95:

# Set environment limits
limit datasize 262144
limit stacksize 32768
setenv TMPDIR `pwd`/tmp                      # /tmp is often not big enough.
setenv SPEC `pwd`
setenv PARALLEL `psrinfo | wc | cut -b 1-10` # For SMP testing.
rm -rf /tmp/prof; mkdir /tmp/prof            # Some config files need this.
rm -rf tmp/*

						- DDH




