You cannot kill a zombied process.  Well, I shouldn't say can't as there is
a trick where you can try to convince a zombie that it is a child of another
parent via the kernel debugger, but that works on a 50-50 scale and can
cuase problems if done improperly.

The only way to clean up defunct procs with a "Z" state is to reboot.

Sorry, its just a fact of UNIX.  This is the same on ALL versions of UNIX
that I know of.

