No, it's not beside aside the issue. I've helped too many
developers/customers
with exactly this problem, which happens exactly for the
reason I stated.
The zombies are there because the parent didn't call wait()
to reap them.
Under SysV, you don't necessarily have to call wait -- you
just
do signal(SIGCHLD, SIG_IGN). Porting this code to a
BSD-based
system causes zombies to be created. Seen it over and over.
End of story.

It may not be why the zombies are there, but it's a decent
possibility.

Jeff




