but turn off the recognition of `readonly' as a token?  It's causing me minor
problems with some OpenSource software that uses `readonly' as a struct member
in several spots.  It's more work to make the code compile in strict mode
than it is to actually change all references to that member to be
`is_readonly', but I was just wondering if the behavior I'm seeing is expected,
and/or documented.

