Running `ar t /some/local/library.a' on a local library always lists an
entry similar to ________64ELEL_.  This isn't mentioned in the ar(1) or
ar(4) man pages (the symdef file is mentioned in the ar(1) man page, but
it's not described in much detail), but it's somewhat documented in the
ar.h header file.  Based on my reading of that header and subsequent
re-readings of ar(1), it's clear that the strange entry I'm seeing is
the symdef entry.

The question is, should doing

	ar -x /some/local/library.a

extract all the object files *and* the symdef file, or just the object
files?

I'm asking because I've run into an OpenSource software package that uses
`ar' to extract all the objects from a local library and then tries to do
something with them, but it fails because it's also getting the symdef
file extracted.  I can easily work around this on a temporary basis, but
I'm wondering if extracting the symdef file is the correct behavior in
the first place.

Tim
