Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Organization: Compaq Computer Corporation
Mime-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

Yes, DEC C provides support for the storage-class modifier readonly,
which is a VAX C keyword. I found a description in section 2.11 or
the DEC C Language Reference Manual.

The fact that it was recognised as a keyword in -std mode for
the DEC C compiler in V4.0D is a feature or a bug, based on your
perspective. The feature/bug is not in the compiler for V4.0F
and later in the -std mode. Admittedly, more users considered
this a bug than a feature...

You could workaround it by adding -Dreadonly=_readonly to your
command line. This essentially is the same as doing this in the
code, prior to the use of readonly:

#define readonly _readonly

Let me know if you need more info.

Thanks,
-Jeff

