Can you please check whether rz4c is the right cd-rom device?
Most of Digital cd-rom device start with RRDxx.

You can use scu command as shown to show the device list.

# scu show edt

CAM Equipment Device Table (EDT) Information:

    Device: RZ28       Bus: 0, Target: 0, Lun: 0, Type: Direct Access
    Device: RZ28       Bus: 0, Target: 1, Lun: 0, Type: Direct Access
    Device: TLZ06      Bus: 0, Target: 2, Lun: 0, Type: Sequential Access
    Device: RZ26       Bus: 0, Target: 3, Lun: 0, Type: Direct Access
    Device: RRD42      Bus: 0, Target: 4, Lun: 0, Type: Read-Only Direct
Access
    Device: RZ28       Bus: 0, Target: 5, Lun: 0, Type: Direct Access

In this case RRD42 is a cd-rom device and map to rz4c.

You always get I/O error if you try to read the disklabel of cd-rom device.
Try file command instead.

# file /dev/rrz4c
/dev/rrz4c: character special (8/4098) SCSI #0 RRD42 disk #32 (SCSI ID #4)
(SCSI LUN #0) offline

Regards,
Somnuk

