Ed Wensell III aka THE StormRaiser wrote:
> 
> Ok, here's my question...
> 
> AlphaServer 2000
> DUNIX 4.0D
> 
> I have connected a VT terminal to the COM1 (tty00) port. So far I am
> able to "throw" (echo "test" > /dev/tty00 works and tail -f [web server
> log] > /dev/tty00 is pretty cool). What I want to do now is simply
> enable logins on this port. Is it possible to do without setting the
> CONSOLE variables from the SRM? Which commands/FAQ should I be lookup
> at?

ACK! Don't touch that! That variable controls which device you wish to
use as a console during SRM and boot operations. What you need is to add
a line in /etc/inittab, like:

terminal:23:respawn:/usr/sbin/getty /dev/tty00 9600 vt100

and issue "init q".

Nix.



