It sounds like you have a corrupted /etc/sia/matrix.conf file.
You should replace it with a good copy.  It's usually a symlink
to one of bsd_matrix.conf or OSFC2_matrix.conf, depending on
which security model you're using.  So, the target of the symlink
is what's `bad'.  I'm sending known good copies of the files in
private email to the poster, just in case that noted system is
the only DEC OSF system available on-site.

