>>>>> On Fri, 12 Feb 1999 15:29:53 GMT, trolin1955@my-dejanews.com said:

trolin1955> Nobody but root can set the executable bit on a file.
trolin1955> That includes copying existing executables, using
trolin1955> linkers, etc.  If one is not root, one cannot make a
trolin1955> file executable.

From a `sysconfig -q vfs noadd-exec-access' on my system:
	vfs:
	noadd-exec-access = 0

On your system, it's almost certainly set to `1' instead of `0'.
Since that parameter is not dynamically reconfigurable, you'll
need to change it in your /etc/sysconfigtab file using
sysconfigdb and then reboot in order to clear this up.

