Things to check,
    Is the variable bootdef_dev set to point to your new external disk ?

    Is the kernel built with support for the SCSI Controller of your boot

    disk?

    Is booting from a device on that controller supported at all ?

    Did you put new bootblocks on the disk using disklabel, before you
    copied the data, or did you try do use dd on the raw devices?

By the way the message about swap is because unix hasn't even got far enough
in the boot to know where it's swap devices are, so don't bother chasing
that
one yet.

Hope this helps,
Adam







