Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

Gottfried Rudorfer <rudorfer@miss.wu-wien.ac.at> wrote:
: i tried to increase the maximum number of open files per process
: under du 4.0e without success.

: i get the error message when the system boots.
: sysconfigtab: attribute open-max-hard in subsystem proc value/size must be <= 40
: 96

: it does not work as described in the du4.0e documentation.
: any hints are welcome. 

solved it here recently with the program below.

see also:
http://www.unix.digital.com/faqs/publications/base_doc/DOCUMENTATION/V40D_HTML/AQTLMCTE/DOCU_002.HTM#ext-file-descript

/* $Source$
 * $Author$ $Date$
 * $Locker$
 * $Revision$
 * File     : "/home/karda/src/misc/setfd64k.c"
 * Creation : "Tue Jan 12 13:37:25 1999 karda"
 * LastEdit : "Thu Jan 14 16:24:02 1999 karda"
 * OS       : "berkeley-unix"
 * Copyright: Bernd Kardatzki, Universitaet Tuebingen, Neuroradiologie
 *            Sektion fuer Experimentelle Kernspinresonanz
 *            72076 Tuebingen, Hoppe-Seylerstr.3
 * Email    : bdkardat@med.uni-tuebingen.de
 * Tel./Fax : (07071) 2980535 / 294371
 * 
 * Synopsis : Change the maximum number of open file descriptors that the
 *            process can have to the highest possible value
 *            and exec() a child process which inherits this property
 *            [DIGITAL UNIX SPECIAL]
 *
 * Status   : done ;)
 *            
 * todo: 
 *       
 */

#define NEW_RLIM_CURR 64*1024
#define NEW_RLIM_MAX  64*1024

#include <stdio.h>
#include <sys/sysinfo.h>
#include <machine/hal_sysinfo.h>
#include <sys/proc.h>
#include <sys/param.h>
#include <sys/resource.h>

int
main(int argc, char **argv){
  int           n;
  int           flag = 1;
  int           fd_newmax;
  struct rlimit rlp;
  char          **newArgv;

  getrlimit(RLIMIT_NOFILE,&rlp);

  printf("active RLIMIT_NOFILE: current=%d,max=%d\n",
         rlp.rlim_cur,rlp.rlim_max);

  getsysinfo(GSI_FD_NEWMAX,&fd_newmax,sizeof(fd_newmax),0,0,0);

  if(fd_newmax==0)
    /* Set utask bit to enable  64K file descriptors support */
    if(setsysinfo(SSI_FD_NEWMAX, NULL, 0, 0, flag))
      perror();
  
  if( (rlp.rlim_cur < NEW_RLIM_CURR ) || (rlp.rlim_max < NEW_RLIM_MAX) ){
    /* Change the values for this process and all of its childs */
    rlp.rlim_cur = NEW_RLIM_CURR;
    rlp.rlim_max = NEW_RLIM_MAX;
    setrlimit(RLIMIT_NOFILE,&rlp);
    getrlimit(RLIMIT_NOFILE,&rlp);
    if((rlp.rlim_cur != NEW_RLIM_CURR ) || (rlp.rlim_max != NEW_RLIM_MAX) )
      fprintf(stderr,"ERROR, COULD NOT SET RLIMIT_NOFILE VALUES TO"
              " current=%d,max=%d.\n"
              "\tActive values are: current=%d,max=%d\n(%s)\n",
              NEW_RLIM_CURR,NEW_RLIM_MAX,rlp.rlim_cur,rlp.rlim_max,strerror(errno));
    else
      printf("changed RLIMIT_NOFILE: current=%d,max=%d\n",
             rlp.rlim_cur,rlp.rlim_max);
  }
  
  if(argc>1){
    newArgv=(char **)malloc(argc * sizeof(char*));
    for(n=1; n<argc; n++)
      newArgv[n-1] = argv[n];
    newArgv[argc-1] = NULL;

    if(execvp(argv[1],newArgv) < 0 ){
      fprintf(stderr,"%s: could not execute '%s' (%s).\n",
              argv[0],argv[1],strerror(errno));
      return -1;
    }
  }
  return 0;
}

