> I got a mail from  Noel LE CORRE( Noel.lecorre@vz.cit.alcatel.fr).He
> suggests  me to use vdump  command which supports dump ADVFS filesystem  to
> a file.

dump -0f /yyydumpfile /xxx

dumps the UFS filesystem /xxx to a disk dump file called "/yyy/dumpfile" 
(well it does on my systems - D.U. V4.0D). If you are talking about
wanting 
to copying filesystem to filesystem, you need to pipe the dump into a
restore (man dump has a nice description of this).
You can also use vdump in the most recent versions of DIGITAL UNIX to
dump
UFS filesets.

Regards,
John Hill
