X-MimeOLE: Produced By Microsoft MimeOLE V4.72.3110.3
Organization: Digital Equipment Corp.
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

Mount it using the following syntax...

# mount -t advfs domain.fileset /mountpoint

you must have /etc/fdmns set up properly to point to the correct disk
partition.

to mount an ADVFS volume on a disk moved from another filesystem
# mkdir /mydisk
# mkdir /etc/fdmns/mydisk
# cd /etc/fdmns/mydisk
# ln -s /dev/rz26h
# moun t -t advfs mydisk#fileset /mydisk

The above mounts an ADVFS fileset called fileset in domain mydisk on
mountpoint /mydisk that uses /dev/rz26h partition

S. Davies

