A warm thank you to Ed Wensell III, who replied in this forum and to
Stanley R Shaw III, who replied by mail.

It would seem that my technique for adding and extra IP-address with the
command

ifconfig lu0 alias xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx

was the correct one. I guess this should also be put in a S00inet file in
/sbin/rc3.d. Any hints there?

Adding another server to the SuiteSpot software turned out to be easy: BIND
the existing server to the existing IP-number, then add another Enterprise
server to the new address.

But as Ed Wensell III aka THE StormRaiser wrote:
> The hardest part will be starting the Administrator if you do not
> already know how.

Well - I did know which port to use. The only problem was that I had no
idea what the admin password was supposed to be (the chap who knew left
under circumstances that would make a request for information, shall we
say, awkward). Alas adding the root:passwordhash from /etc/passwd to the
admpw file did the trick.

Again: Thank you for the help. It was highly appreciated

Cheers

