Subject: Re: PWS500au power management
Date: 1999/02/05
Message-ID: <36BB4C9B.29367D89@zk3.dec.com>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 441106451
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
References: <36B637B4.6CE686A2@ULeth.ca> <36B63F8B.41C6@umich.edu>
X-Accept-Language: en
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Organization: CTG
Mime-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

You can set this permanently in yout /etc/sysconfigtab file so that it
doesn't ever happen with the following script.

Once you do this evertime your system boots it will retain these settings
and there is no need to do this in a cron job.

The sysconfigdb -s synchronizes the /etc/sysconfigtab file with the incore
values.

Check out the sysconfigdb man page.


Sean

#!/bin/sh

cat <<=EOD= >/etc/sysconfigtab.local

pwrmgr:
        disk_spindown = 0
        disk_dwell_time = 0

=EOD=

sysconfigdb -f /etc/sysconfigtab.local -m pwrmgr
sysconfigdb -s



