Hi,

The use of the "hiprof" command, instead of the "atom" command
suggests that the Atom ADK (ATMBASE400) was installed and used.
The problem looks like a bug in the ADK, so if you de-install
the ADK (with setld -d), the problem may be resolved.

However, note that even the official hiprof's -cputime option has 
proven inaccurate with some threaded programs, because it uses the
Alpha RPCC instruction to access the cycle counter, and this counter
can not be reliably mapped to user-level pthreads. So, expect the
option to be unavailable for threaded programs in future releases 
and patch kits. A new PC-sampling technique has been developed to
replace the -cputime option, and rollout plans are underway.

Thanks
	John P Williams, Unix development environment group, Compaq



