Arum Han <hana@email.uc.edu> writes:

>We are using Digital unix 4.0A on a alphastation 255.
>It's using NFS filesystem and it uses automount function but
>I can't find which file is the configuration file for automounting.

One of the networking manuals has a fairly decent description.

Basically, automount looks for the NIS map auto.master first, then
/etc/auto.master, IIRC.  (I use -m -f /usr/local/auto.standard to avoid
our NIS database.)

>so the filesystem is always mounted.
>So, I want to know where I can configure the automount and where
>it is started

Explore:

# grep -l automount /sbin/*.d/* 
/sbin/init.d/nfsmount
/sbin/rc0.d/K35nfsmount
/sbin/rc2.d/K40nfsmount
/sbin/rc3.d/S20nfsmount

>Second thing is, when digital unix is booting, which file is used for
>configuration?
>/etc/rc.config and /sbin/rc3, is that all?

And lotsa other files.  Try "ls -lrt /etc" and look at files modified since
installation.

>I want to add a command to launch the apache webserver when the system
>reboots.

Create your own /sbin/init.d script and link it into /sbin/rc*.d.
