john.allen@geonet-tech.com (John Allen) writes:

>I have a PC application which uses rsh to 'connect' to my alpha's DAT
>drive for backing up PC drives.  I'm getting an error whenever I
>attempt to perform the operation.  The vendor suggests that rshd
>should be running(and is not) on my Alpha.  In fact rshd is NOT
>running as a daemon process on the Alpha - should it be?  Or, can I
>install it as a running daemon?  How?

Rshd is a process that is usually started from inetd.  One daemon is
started for each reqeusts and it exits when the request is done.

Rshd works with poor authentication, but some authentication nonetheless.

You'll need a ~/.rhosts file setup for rshd to work.

Casper
