Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

I would like to thank all those who replied to my message. The method which
worked for me was given by Thomas Leitner:

#mount -u /
#cd /etc/fdmns
#mkdir usr_domain
#ln -s /dev/rz16g
#mount usr_domain#usr /tmp/tom

This enabled me to mount the drive, delete the core files then I was able to
boot the system normally.

Thanks
Tommy
tfoley@eng.uab.edu

